iOS native views: the app's UIView shown beneath GPUI's non-opaque CAMetalLayer, through gpui_apple's hole (needs 0049, 0050 and 0059-0061).

What:
- `IosWindow::attach_native_view` puts the view in a clipping container inserted directly below GPUI's view; `draw`
  plans each scene's placements (gpui_apple's shared `plan_layout` and `Placement`, 0059, from core's
  `native_view_placement`, 0050: `visible`, `background`), presents with `draw_placing_native_views` (0060: in step
  whenever the scene moves, resizes, shows, hides or restacks a view) and then applies them in one no-animation block
  (frames, hidden, and `NativeView::set_background`'s colour on the host view behind them), then restacks, as macOS's
  native_views.rs does. A view is hidden in a scene that doesn't paint it and removed when its last handle drops.
- `native_view_input` is `Window`: GPUI's view stays on top and takes every touch, so pointer and scroll over a view
  reach its element's listeners; the view gets none unless the app forwards it.

Where: a new file, ios/window/native_views.rs (attach, plan, apply), behind one-line hooks in upstream's window.rs.
The containers and the colour go in GPUI's view's superview; until 0063 nests GPUI's view in a host view, that is
the window itself.

Why: upstream's `NativeView::new` fails on iOS. Lifecycle, clipping and z-order follow Flutter's
FlutterPlatformViewsController.mm (oracle only: Flutter draws over its views, this draws under them; its touch
interceptor is the model for an app that forwards touches into its view). The attach and apply code is gpui_macos's
window/native_views.rs (upstream GPUI, Apache-2.0) adapted to UIKit, which is most of this patch's size; as a
near-verbatim port of proven code it is exempt from the size limit (patch rule 4).

Checked (0062–0064 together) on the iOS 26.5 simulator (iPhone 17 at 3x, iPad Air 11-inch at 2x) with
examples/native-view and scripts/apple-native-view-checks.sh: 0 GPUI frames/s while the view recolours at 63
frames/s; every recorded frame shows the view and the div over it with no gap pixel, still and with the slot moving
every frame.

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

